-- ~/.hammerspoon/init.lua (managed by chezmoi: home/dot_hammerspoon/init.lua.tmpl)
--
-- Reactive window-to-display and space placement with per-docking-state presets.
--
-- A `preset` maps bundle-id -> list of screen indices (1-indexed, left-to-right).
-- A `spaceLayout` maps bundle-id -> list of space indices within that screen.
-- The Nth window for an app uses preset[bid][N] and spaceLayout[bid][N], wrapping.
--
-- Active preset is chosen automatically from connected display count:
--   1 screen  -> "laptop"    (3 spaces: comms | dev | support)
--   2 screens -> "minimal"
--   3+ screens -> "office"   (pin to "homeoffice" manually when at home)
--
-- IPC (call via `hs -c '<fn>()'`):
--   preset("office"|"homeoffice"|"minimal"|"laptop")  -- pin a preset
--   preset("auto")                                    -- release pin
--   currentPreset()                                   -- name + screen count
--   commApps()                                        -- launch comm-app set
--   snapAll()                                         -- re-snap every window
--   hs.reload()                                       -- reload init.lua
--
-- Amethyst handles sizing within each display; this script decides
-- WHICH display and WHICH space a window lives on.

